":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T14:24:31-07:00","id":1540144,"title":"","content":"I still enjoy Van Damme's Timecop.<br /> <br /> Universal Soldier is also pretty good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T17:08:42-07:00","id":1540153,"title":"","content":"Yes Timecop and Universal Soldier the first one were the best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T17:57:48-07:00","id":1540157,"title":"","content":"I have a long-standing fondness for the early 80s sci fi film <b>Battle Beyond the Stars</b>. Made by Roger Corman's studio to cash in on the popularity of Star Wars, it is literally The Magnificent Seven in space. Not only does it have George Peppard in the role he auditioned for in The Magnificent Seven but didn't get, it also has Robert Vaughn <i>playing the same character he played in the original film</i>. The special effects are also pretty good for a film of its nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T18:08:08-07:00","id":1540158,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say Universal Soldier is a guilty pleasure. The first one is an actual classic and a good movie, and it's maybe the best use of Van Damme's inability to act. He is exactly the actor the character needs, non ironic.<br /> <br /> And that reminds me again of Street Fighter. Where Raul Julia was the highlight of the movie, the only good acting in it, it's maybe Van Damme's worse performance as Guile, and either way he's the worse in an already bad movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T19:33:21-07:00","id":1540163,"title":"","content":"Without going to much off topic. One could argue that watching Jean Claude Van Damme act is a guilty pleasure as he is limited but he had a great charm that we loved and allowed us to overlook that fact and he has gotten better bin his later years and sticks to roles that play to that charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T19:44:15-07:00","id":1540164,"title":"","content":"Ninja 3 The Domination is another Cannon Films classic of low budget action films that were light on story. For reasons unexplained the ninja baddie kills a number of people on a golf course and nearly gets killed by the police and slips away from them and staggered into a female phone operator and places his essence into her.<br /> <br /> The hero played by Sho Kosigi with an eye patch arrives at the morgue and somehow knows what ritual was performed and takes the body to a Asian temple and graciously fixed up the body when the evil ninja returns.<br /> <br /> The lady know being influenced by the evil ninja spirit is killing off the cops who had a hand in his death including one that she is dating.<br /> <br /> Sho is able to reach her and drive out the spirit and we have battle between the two of them that involves fireballs, controlling monks and drilling through the ground before Sho finally killed him for good.<br /> <br /> Cannon Films started my love for martial arts action films and seeing how cheesy they were is fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-05-2025, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T04:23:07-07:00","id":1540426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1539775-guilty-pleasure-viewing?p=1540144#post1540144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still enjoy Van Damme's Timecop.<br /> <br /> Universal Soldier is also pretty good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Universal Soldier is great!<br /> <br /> Timecop is ok... but the time travel rules don't make a lot of sense, so I get hung up on that sometimes. LOL. It's not bad though..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1539775-guilty-pleasure-viewing?p=1540164#post1540164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ninja 3 The Domination is another Cannon Films classic of low budget action films that were light on story. For reasons unexplained the ninja baddie kills a number of people on a golf course and nearly gets killed by the police and slips away from them and staggered into a female phone operator and places his essence into her.<br /> <br /> The hero played by Sho Kosigi with an eye patch arrives at the morgue and somehow knows what ritual was performed and takes the body to a Asian temple and graciously fixed up the body when the evil ninja returns.<br /> <br /> The lady know being influenced by the evil ninja spirit is killing off the cops who had a hard in his death including one that she is dating.<br /> <br /> Sho is able to reach her and drive out the spirit and we have battle between the two of them that involves fireballs, controlling monks and drilling through the ground before Sho finally killed him for good.<br /> <br /> Cannon Films started my love for martial arts action films and seeing how cheesy they were is fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I bought a blu-ray of that not too long ago and revisited it. It's still pretty fun! I watched it a TON back in the day, so I'm glad it was still a fun movie to watch.<br /> <br /> Pray for Death is another great Ninja movie I used to watch a ton and revisited recently. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T12:28:53-07:00","id":1540458,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to look for more older Sho Kosigi films to watch and seeing him in the Cannon films brings back a smile to my face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T12:37:48-07:00","id":1540463,"title":"","content":"The original Road House with the late Patrick Swayze and the always cool Sam Elliot. Everyone knew that this film was going to be a popcorn movie and not win any awards or much else and was depending on the great charm and physical presence of Patrick Swayze and it worked like a charm.","signature":"<hr cl