s he was making go up in smoke and see the Andrew Scott clone acting more human then the others despite the second hand mental trauma that he gained from his doner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T15:25:01-07:00","id":1541808,"title":"","content":"This is slightly different, but I think that Jesse Eisenberg had the potential to have been a great Lex Luthor when he was cast. I had seen him play similar character in Now You Can See Me and I thought it was perfect casting in that regard.<br /> <br /> Alas the Synder stuff wasn't all that great and good actors like Cavill and Eisenberg can only do much with the material given.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T23:32:37-07:00","id":1542163,"title":"","content":"There is this odd subgenre of 1990s science fiction films that I greatly enjoy, that being the &quot;the end of the millennium is going to be violent and crazy and slightly absurd, especially in Los Angeles&quot; movie trend. The opening scene of <i>Demolition Man</i> is part of it, as is <i>Predator 2</i>. Another is <b>Virtuosity</b>, a quasi-cyberpunk thing with Denzel Washington and Russell Crowe that I think is unfairly forgotten. Released about the same time was <b>Strange Days</b>, which sadly underperformed at the box office thanks in large part to a really terrible and obtuse trailer. (And it continues to infuriate me that neither this nor director Kathryn Bigelow's other cult classic <i>Near Dark</i> have ever been released on blu ray, not even after her Oscar win.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T08:37:16-07:00","id":1542176,"title":"","content":"Strange Days is one of the better underrated science fiction films of the 1990's and as for Virtuosity I couldn't really like the film despite the casting of Denzel Washington and Russell Crowe or the always good William Forsythe who played Denzel's former captain in the LAPD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T04:22:32-07:00","id":1542242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1539775-guilty-pleasure-viewing?p=1542163#post1542163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Released about the same time was <b>Strange Days</b>, which sadly underperformed at the box office thanks in large part to a really terrible and obtuse trailer. (And it continues to infuriate me that neither this nor director Kathryn Bigelow's other cult classic <i>Near Dark</i> have ever been released on blu ray, not even after her Oscar win.)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1539775-guilty-pleasure-viewing?p=1542176#post1542176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strange Days is one of the better underrated science fiction films of the 1990's</div> </div> </div> </div>I love Strange Days!! I've been watching it every year on New Years Eve for I don't know how long... it's great! Crazy how relevant it still is.<br /> <br /> Sucks there hasn't been a blu-ray release of it. But, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> , Near Dark did get a blu-ray release, at least briefly, because I have it! The cover is awful, but I'm still glad I was able to get it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T13:26:24-07:00","id":1542267,"title":"","content":"Most of the blu ray releases of Near Dark I've seen are European ones, but apparently yes there was a blink and you'll miss it US release in 2009. I really hope someone like Arrow Video can pick up the rights to do a good 4K version (one that keeps James Cameron as far away as possible).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T15:34:49-07:00","id":1542276,"title":"","content":"What did James Cameron do to Near Dark that you want him no where near any DVD/Blu Ray package?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T15:35:48-07:00","id":1542277,"title":"","content":"Other than the fact that his ex wife Kathryn Bigelow was behind the film?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T16:53:29-07:00","id":1542279,"title":"","content":"The recent 4K releases of Cameron's catalog, including Terminator 2, Aliens, and True Lies, all of which he personally oversaw and approved, heavily used AI to alter the films in numerous ways. Generally speaking, Cameron apparently wants all of them to look like the completely digital imagery of his Avatar movies instead of something actually shot on physical film, and essentially threw a tantrum when a number of physical media collectors and film aficionados - ie, the people who actually buy 4K - complained about it. <br /> <br /> (I have heard, but not confirmed, that the alterations to Aliens actually make the puppeteers operating the xenomorphs visible in certain scenes.)<br /> <br /> But at any rate, thankfully Cameron had no involvement in Near Dark, aside from IIRC a small cameo. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T18:35:03-07:00","id":1542281,"title":"","content":"So James Cameron is in some ways is becoming like George Lucas when it comes to his older work and making unneeded changes to his films.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T19:16:58-07:00","id":1542286,"title":"","content":"Dorian. A film from around 2003 that stars Malcolm McDowell as the only big name in it.<br /> <br /> Here we have a photographer named Louis who encounters a modeling agency by Henri played by Malcolm McDowell and signs him up and tells his new client about Dorian Gray and said guy wishes it was true. Not knowing that Malcolm McDowell is the devil and grants the Wish.<br /> <br /> So for thirty years Louis goes on a endless orgy of drugs, alcohol and women and noticed that he isn't ageing and a photo of him is showing all the years of toll.<br /> <br /> Our protagonist isn't all that bright when it comes to details such as everyone around him is aging except him and ...... Henri played by Malcolm McDowell. You just think that he would pick up on the fact that Henri his agent looks exactly the same.<br /> <br /> I enjoyed the film mostly because of Malcolm McDowell scenes as he was the only good thing in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T12:51:19-07:00","id":1542383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1539775-guilty-pleasure-viewing?p=1542267#post1542267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the blu ray releases of Near Dark I've seen are European ones, but apparently yes there was a blink and you'll miss it US release in 2009. I really hope someone like Arrow Video can pick up the rights to do a good 4K version (one that keeps James Cameron as far away as possible).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yea, I'm with! Really hoping someone like Arrow will put out a great 4k version of Near Dark and Strange Days! That'd be so awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T12:54:43-07:00","id":1542384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1539775-guilty-pleasure-viewing?p=1542279#post1542279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The recent 4K releases of Cameron's catalog, including Terminator 2, Aliens, and True Lies, all of which he personally oversaw and approved, heavily used AI to alter the films in numerous ways. Generally speaking, Cameron apparently wants all of them to look like the completely digital imagery of his Avatar movies instead of something actually shot on physical film, and essentially threw a tantrum when a number of physical media collectors and film aficionados - ie, the people who actually buy 4K - complained about it.<br /> <br /> (I have heard, but not confirmed, that the alterations to Aliens actually make the puppeteers operating the xenomorphs visible in certain scenes.)<br /> <br /> But at any rate, thankfully Cameron had no involvement in Near Dark, aside from IIRC a small cameo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I watched the Aliens 4K a bit back ago and I don't remembering see the puppeteers... but maybe I need to rewatch and pay closer attention.<br /> <br /> I have the 4K for True Lies, since there wasn't a blu-ray release prior, and it's not as good as one would hope. It's not absolutely terrible, but there are times the digital noise reduction they did looks pretty bad.<br /> <br /> Why Cameron doesn't want to do a proper restoration is beyond me...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T13:58:15-07:00","id":1542391,"title":"","content":"My layman's understanding is that True Lies was shot on a specific type of 35mm camera set up that was designed to make it easier to adapt the footage for television and VHS release at the time but ends up having some issues when doing a transfer to more modern DVD/BR and wide screen TV formats. Bigelow's Point Break was shot using the same type of camera, and apparently the recent Shout Factory release shows those issues when you try to do it unaltered. But the True Lies 4K ends up overcorrecting to the point where it looks like a movie made in the past five or ten years instead of a film made in the 1990s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T14:22:15-07:00","id":1542395,"title":"","content":"Regarding guilty pleasure TV shows, I have a lifelong fondness for Friday the 13th The Series. Part of the slew of late 80s/early 90s syndicated science fiction tv shows, it has nothing to do with the more famous film series other than sharing a producer, Frank Mancuso Jr. Instead, it follows the adventures of a pair of cousins who have inherited their creepy uncle's antiques store only to find that most of the stuff he sold was cursed by the devil at leave death and misery in their wake. So they spend most of their time trying to recover cursed antiques. <br /> It is a cheesy series, with a lot of the dodgy practical special effects and melodramatics of both &quot;Technicolor Gothic&quot; era tv and episodical sci fi shows. However, this show helped nurture my lifelong enjoyment of both horror and history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T17:09:12-07:00","id":1542400,"title":"","content":"I remembered the Friday The 13th series with Uncle Louis who sold his soul to the devil to become a successful shop owner and would curse the items that his friend Jack Marshack would get for him. Then felt some regret and tried to get out of the deal but couldn't and left his store to his cousins when the devil came collecting. I can't believe that I remembered the names of two of the more interesting characters of the show and not the two who played the cousins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-18-2024, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-19T05:49:21-07:00","id":1542422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1539775-guilty-pleasure-viewing?p=1542391#post1542391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My layman's understanding is that True Lies was shot on a specific type of 35mm camera set up that was designed to make it easier to adapt the footage for television and VHS release at the time but ends up having some issues when doing a transfer to more modern DVD/BR and wide screen TV formats. Bigelow's Point Break was shot using the same type of camera, and apparently the recent Shout Factory release shows those issues when you try to do it unaltered. But the True Lies 4K ends up overcorrecting to the point where it looks like a movie made in the past five or ten years instead of a film made in the 1990s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! I didn't know that about the way they shot those movies. Interesting... I hadn't seen that 4K transfer of Point Break yet. But yea, that True Lies 4K is weird in spots and makes the people look a little plasticy....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T12:13:34-07:00","id":1542490,"title":"","content":"I remembered a sci-fi show from the early 1990's called Time Trax that was set I like in the late 22nd century that had a cop who had to go back in time because a evil scientist sent a huge number of criminals into the late 20th century and that couldn't be allowed to stand as they could influence history. The special effects were so so for a tv show of it's time and it only lasted a season and a half.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T09:20:23-07:00","id":1543062,"title":"","content":"Another guilty pleasure is watching Malcolm McDowell films where you know that he is the only real good thing to see on the screen.<br /> <br /> For example the two or so minutes that he is in Cyborg 3 is the only worthwhile stuff to see. Everyone else is awful and didn't make it big.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T07:07:20-07:00","id":1544842,"title":"","content":"Lord of Illusions was awesome; it came out at about the same time we were playing M:tA. &quot;I have all this power to give you and all you have to do is beg&quot;. That quote was gnarly back then!<br /> <br /> I liked Strange Days, but now, I don't think I'd watch it again.<br /> <br /> So, we had a VCR-descrambler, so we could record movies we got from the video-rental stores. I remember going there, picked a movie, and watching it / recording it to see if I like it. Three movies to a tape.<br /> <br /> I've watched Death Proof a lot, just for the conversations-dialogs.<br /> <br /> When I was a kid, I used to watch Aliens (on Beta) over and over again, just mainly because i liked the set. Screamers also comes to mind. <br /> <br /> Wasn't Battlefield-Earth written by a guy that created his own religion as a tax-scheme?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T20:38:19-07:00","id":1544951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1539775-guilty-pleasure-viewing?p=1544842#post1544842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lord of Illusions was awesome; it came out at about the same time we were playing M:tA. &quot;I have all this power to give you and all you have to do is beg&quot;. That quote was gnarly back then!<br /> <br /> I liked Strange Days, but now, I don't think I'd watch it again.<br /> <br /> So, we had a VCR-descrambler, so we could record movies we got from the video-rental stores. I remember going there, picked a movie, and watching it / recording it to see if I like it. Three movies to a tape.<br /> <br /> I've watched Death Proof a lot, just for the conversations-dialogs.<br /> <br /> When I was a kid, I used to watch Aliens (on Beta) over and over again, just mainly because i liked the set. Screamers also comes to mind.<br /> <br /> Wasn't Battlefield-Earth written by a guy that created his own religion as a tax-scheme?</div> </div> </div> </div>L. Ron Hubbard reportedly started Scientology as part of a bet with Robert Heinlein about who could manage making their works into a religion first. Heinlein had scruples and put a stop to things on his end; Hubbard didn't... and didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-31T13:25:40-07:00","id":1545101,"title":"","content":"I have heard the same story about L. Ron Hubbard saying that making a religion was good way to make money and sadly if true as his Scientology group is still around and making trouble for folks who call out his cons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T11:39:27-08:00","id":1545262,"title":"","content":"Mr. Brooks with Kevin Costner is a underrated film that doesn't get enough attention &amp; I feel that it was his best work at the time and thought Demi Moore was a good foil against him. I get the notion that other films were planned for Mr. Brooks and his daughter but because of the lack of commercial success of the film the plans were scrapped.<br /> <br /> In the long run it might've been a good thing as the sequel might've been mediocre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T04:20:42-08:00","id":1545379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1539775-guilty-pleasure-viewing?p=1545262#post1545262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mr. Brooks with Kevin Costner is a underrated film that doesn't get enough attention &amp; I feel that it was his best work at the time and thought Demi Moore was a good foil against him. I get the notion that other films were planned for Mr. Brooks and his daughter but because of the lack of commercial success of the film the plans were scrapped.<br /> <br /> In the long run it might've been a good thing as the sequel might've been mediocre.</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved Mr. Brooks! I was starting to think I was the only one that remembered it. LOL!<br /> <br /> I thought Kevin Costner did an amazing job as a serial killer, and William Hurt was great as the devil on his shoulder.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what they would have done with a sequel though, so I'm kinda glad they didn't do it. I guess they could have focused on the daughter (played by Danielle Panabaker) which could be interesting. But, I think it works good as a stand alone movie..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T10:05:24-08:00","id":1545395,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly is that the people behind Mr. Brooks were pretty new to the business and Kevin Costner was a big champion for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 11-07-2024, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T20:17:11-08:00","id":1545429,"title":"","content":"Another guilty pleasure film is the Guy Pearce, Jeremy Irons and Orlando Jones film The Time Machine that was based somewhat on H.G. Wells book.<br /> <br /> Certainly it wasn't as good as the film a few decades earlier, but I found it enjoyable and giving a dead girlfriend as the motivation for the Doctor to create a time machine to save her and find that his efforts were fruitless and going further into the future to figure out why and seeing a Victorian Era person reaction to a society that would be unthinkable to him.<br /> <br /> Then we have Orlando Jones as a artificial intelligence that survives the end of the old world and us still around nearly a million years later with no real clue as to why. Perhaps the Morlocks machines were unknowingly keeping him around and the fact that he didn't go insane during this time is surprising.<br /> <br /> Then you have Jeremy Irons playing a Uber Morlock who explained why the Doctor can never save his girlfriend as it would create a paradox as it was her death that gave him the idea for the time machine and had she lived,. He would never come up with the idea and how could he go back in time to save her.<br /> <br /> This is why time travel stories are so headache inducing.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T23:06:36-08:00","id":1545441,"title":"","content":"True Blood for all its blood, nudity, and vampirism.<br /> <br /> Game of Thrones for the same except replace vampirism with hereditary privilege.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T16:10:09-08:00","id":1545498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1539775-guilty-pleasure-viewing?p=1545429#post1545429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another guilty pleasure film is the Guy Pearce, Jeremy Irons and Orlando Jones film The Time Machine that was based somewhat on H.G. Wells book.<br /> <br /> Certainly it wasn't as good as the film a few decades earlier, but I found it enjoyable and giving a dead girlfriend as the motivation for the Doctor to create a time machine to save her and find that his efforts were fruitless and going further into the future to figure out why and seeing a Victorian Era person reaction to a society that would be unthinkable to him.<br /> <br /> Then we have Orlando Jones as a artificial intelligence that survives the end of the old world and us still around nearly a million years later with no real clue as to why. Perhaps the Morlocks machines were unknowingly keeping him around and the fact that he didn't go insane during this time is surprising.<br /> <br /> Then you have Jeremy Irons playing a Uber Morlock who explained why the Doctor can never save his girlfriend as it would create a paradox as it was her death that gave him the idea for the time machine and had she lived,. He would never come up with the idea and how could he go back in time to save her.<br /> <br /> This is why time travel stories are so headache inducing.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I love time travel stories! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And this version of The Time Machine isn't bad. I kinda liked it. And I love some of the world building, like the lunar mining disaster...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.driv