Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-10T16:05:57-08:00","id":1545661,"title":"","content":"I think Clash of the Titans remake and the later sequel Wrath of the Titans might be considered guilty pleasure viewing by now. But I can't watch one without watching the other right after. especially before a Scion game...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T04:35:26-08:00","id":1545685,"title":"","content":"I have no guilty pleasures, but I do have a lot of unpopular opinions when it comes to media.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I unironically love the epic film Gods &amp; Generals","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T10:07:34-08:00","id":1545704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1539775-guilty-pleasure-viewing?p=1545644#post1545644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Crow remake was dead on arrival when it was first announced by Hollywood to be fair. Nobody was asking for it to be made and you knew it from the trailer and character descriptions in the movie that the character was unlikable and bland.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1539775-guilty-pleasure-viewing?p=1545658#post1545658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Crow post would fit better under the vent post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I considered putting the post there... but this one was all about movies, so I wasn't totally sure. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yea, the crazy thing it's not even really a remake. There is nothing, aside from the title and two character names, that are even remotely close to the original movie. Blows my mind...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-11T14:33:37-08:00","id":1545712,"title":"","content":"Dracula 3 The Legacy is something of major guilty pleasure. The story is pretty weak and cheaply made as it was shot in Romania for cost reasons. It's a sequel to the Dracula 2000 movie which was pretty bad itself.<br /> <br /> The best thing in the third Dracula film is that it was played by the late Rutger Hauer who showed in in the third act and improvised his dialogue as what was written must have been pretty awful. Rutger Hauer would have made a good Dracula if given a good script.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-18T13:37:18-08:00","id":1546082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1539775-guilty-pleasure-viewing?p=1545641#post1545641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, I know this isn't necessarily the right thread for this, but I watched the Crow remake recently and it was unbelievably bad. I had pretty low expectation going in and it was even worse than I expected.<br /> <br /> When I first heard about it it was billed as being close to the original comic, but after the first trailer I knew that was an outright lie. But, I liked the other Crow movies for the most part, so I hoped maybe we'd at least get an interning entry in the series. But it's awful. And kind of boring. There's essentially one action scene, and it's not too bad, but aside from that there isn't much happening. I couldn't believe how bad it was..<br /> <br /> Anyway, just had to warn y'all. LOL.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, the Crow remake sucked. Although I toss it into the same bucket as Madame Web and Venom 3 as far as 2024 is concerned. Boring, unsatisfying and disappointing - but above all utterly uninteresting. I doubt I will ever think about these again.<br /> <br /> The two bad movies from 2024, though, I'm still wrestling with are Joker 2 and Megalopolis. At least, those two are bad in interesting ways! With Joker 2 you have a movie whose whole message is that people who want to see this kind of movie are bad people. A kind of &quot;fuck you&quot; to the audience saying &quot;What do you expect? It's a mentally ill person having a miserable time. There's nothing extraordinary happening here.&quot; You have that on one hand, this movie trying to give the audience the middle finger but on the other hand - why did you make the movie then? And this isn't an indie-movie. Todd Philipps had 200 million dollars to play around with. This movie had musical-scenes and he cast Lady Gaga in it! All that to say he feels disappointed in people who want to see this movie...? Still wrestling with that one.<br /> <br /> The other one is Megalopolis... Haha, now there's a BAD-bad movie if there ever was one. It's more like a fever dream, I guess - but not in any way that's fun.<br /> <br /> Just look at this for a taste of what it's like to watch Megalopolis:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tNybhMsO5ew\" data-code=\"tNybhMsO5ew\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/tNybhMsO5ew/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Strangely I think Adam Driver actually gives a good performance in this movie. He's on the same wavelength as this psychotic fever-dream coming to you straight from Francis Ford Coppola's decrepit mind. The other one who really gets it is Aubrey Plaza in her role as (I shit you not) Wow Platinum. Yep, that's her character's name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-18T13:42:39-08:00","id":1546083,"title":"","content":"Adam Driver is a good actor when he is given a good script to work with. I thought his work in 65 and Logan Lucky were quite excellent and he was the only worthwhile thing in the Star Wars sequels but they changed the character arc for Kylo Ren according to a old interview he done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-18T13:45:57-08:00","id":1546084,"title":"","content":"Going back to Revenge of the Ninja, Another thing that stood out to me that I didn't care at age 10 when I first saw the film. The bad guy in the film Branden the silver mask ninja shouldn't have lasted as long as he did as his mask while it looked cool as hell. It would severely limit his depth perception and periphail vision and he would forever bumping into things like Michael Keaton said when he wore the Batman suit and how a six year old could beat him up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-18T14:30:41-08:00","id":1546089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1539775-guilty-pleasure-viewing?p=1546083#post1546083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adam Driver is a good actor when he is given a good script to work with. I thought his work in 65 and Logan Lucky were quite excellent and he was the only worthwhile thing in the Star Wars sequels but they changed the character arc for Kylo Ren according to a old interview he done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I wasn't a fan of 65. All that dinosaur-action... Adam Driver wasn't bad in it, though. It made me think of A Sound of Thunder (2005). Do you remember that one? Not a good movie by any stretch of the imagination. But that one was also all about travelling to the past and messing around with dinosaurs.<br /> <br /> And Logan Lucky was good, I thought.<br /> <br /> As for Kylo Ren... Yeah, sure... But I don't blame any of the actors for that one. Hopefully, some years down the line a journalist will do a comprehensive postmortem on it and how they got it all wrong over there at Disney.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-19T04:23:21-08:00","id":1546124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1539775-guilty-pleasure-viewing?p=1546082#post1546082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, the Crow remake sucked. Although I toss it into the same bucket as Madame Web and Venom 3 as far as 2024 is concerned. Boring, unsatisfying and disappointing - but above all utterly uninteresting. I doubt I will ever think about these again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't seen Venom 3 yet, but yea, Madame Web wasn't good. It had a few interesting moments, but that movie was a mess.<br /> <br /> And yea, I was just shocked at how bad that Crow movie was...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1539775-guilty-pleasure-viewing?p=1546082#post1546082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The two bad movies from 2024, though, I'm still wrestling with are Joker 2 and Megalopolis. At least, those two are bad in interesting ways! With Joker 2 you have a movie whose whole message is that people who want to see this kind of movie are bad people. A kind of &quot;fuck you&quot; to the audience saying &quot;What do you expect? It's a mentally ill person having a miserable time. There's nothing extraordinary happening here.&quot; You have that on one hand, this movie trying to give the audience the middle finger but on the other hand - why did you make the movie then? And this isn't an indie-movie. Todd Philipps had 200 million dollars to play around with. This movie had musical-scenes and he cast Lady Gaga in it! All that to say he feels disappointed in people who want to see this movie...? Still wrestling with that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I watched it this past weekend, and yea, it wasn't great. Again, there were some interesting moments, and the ending kind of shocked me. But over all there really much happening in it. I can't believe they didn't more with Lady Gaga.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1539775-guilty-pleasure-viewing?p=1546082#post1546082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other one is Megalopolis... Haha, now there's a BAD-bad movie if there ever was one. It's more like a fever dream, I guess - but not in any way that's fun.<br /> <br /> Strangely I think Adam Driver actually gives a good performance in this movie. He's on the same wavelength as this psychotic fever-dream coming to you straight from Francis Ford Coppola's decrepit mind. The other one who really gets it is Aubrey Plaza in her role as (I shit you not) Wow Platinum. Yep, that's her character's name.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen this one yet, but again, I haven't heard great things. I do like Adam Driver and Aubrey Plaza, so I might check it out for them, but the movie itself sounds super weird and not in a good way.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD 